This is a Copywest license. It uses the creator's underlying ownership to grant 
specific, conditional open freedoms to the general public while maintaining a 
strict legal firewall around the core creation.

1. RETAINED OWNERSHIP:
All copyright and intellectual property rights belong strictly to the original 
creator, Oliver James Mckimmie. The creator retains 100% ownership of the original 
design elements, code lines, internal architecture, unique inventions, and all future 
core modifications, contributions, and forks. This ownership does not extend to 
unrelated, independent components created around the product.

2. THE "ALWAYS OPEN" PUBLIC RULE:
The general public is granted the right to copy, view, utilize, and modify this 
Base Product. Any changes, fixes, or optimizations made directly to the internal 
elements of this Base Product MUST be made publicly available and remain 100% 
visible and free to everyone under this exact Copywest license.

3. THE "EXTERNAL PRODUCT" EXCEPTION (WEAK RECIPROCITY):
Subject to the strict commercial bans in Section 4, if a non-commercial creator 
incorporates this Base Product cleanly as an independent component inside a larger 
External Product without modifying the internal elements of the Base Product itself, 
the Copywest openness rules do NOT apply to the surrounding components. All rights 
remain strictly reserved to that creator for their custom External Product elements.

4. COMMERCIAL BANS, CONVERSION, AND REPLICATION LOOPHOLES:
Hobbyists and individuals are free to utilize this Product under the open terms 
above. However, commercial businesses, corporations, and for-profit entities are 
STRICTLY PROHIBITED from using this Product, any code inside it, or any part of it. 

Businesses are explicitly banned from:
- Converting, translating, compiling, or processing any part of this code into a 
  hardware design, GPU configuration, integrated circuit layout, or FPGA bitstream.
- Copying the product's design structure and simply changing what it does or altering 
  its target function to bypass this license.
- Manufacturing, designing, or distributing any individual component that is based 
  on, or derived from, the unique inventions created by this Product.

If a business wants rights to use, modify, replicate, or build components from any 
part of this design for any purpose, they MUST obtain explicit written permission 
and a commercial agreement from Oliver James Mckimmie.

5. AUTOMATIC TERMINATION:
Any attempt to hide modifications made to the Base Product itself, or any 
unauthorized commercial use, conversion, or functional replication, results in the 
